name: "AiR-Poet"
type: "system"
about: "
AiR-Poet is the runtime implementation of the AiR intermediary representation language.

AiR is a table-based Lisp with lazy evaluation, mixed indexing, and scope inheritance,
designed as a target language for deterministic AI code generation via the META methodology.

## Architecture

AiR-Poet is a pipeline:

  source text
    → tokenizer   (lexical analysis, flat token stream)
    → parser      (token stream → AST)
    → ast_node    (AST data model / node types)
    → interpreter (tree-walk evaluator)
    → prelude     (built-in functions, operators, standard environment)
    → repl        (interactive session)

## File Conventions

Each component follows the same layout:
  <name>.meta   — specification (this format)
  <name>.air    — AiR language definition of the component
  <name>.py     — Python implementation
  plan_<name>.md — design rationale and decisions
  test.py / test.air — tests

## Related Systems

  air_meta/   — META methodology implementation (consensus-driven AI code generation)
  air_vm/     — AiR virtual machine (bytecode or direct AST execution)
"

components: {
    air
    tokenizer
    parser
    ast_node
    interpreter
    prelude
    repl
    air_meta
    air_vm
}
